From c3951ced53c5dfbf51d2f6143546201861b67b12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:22:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(sessions): record child sessions started through the
 Agent API

Add a nullable sessions.parent_session_id (idempotent migration plus
index), separate from fork lineage, so an orchestrator's worker sessions
can be nested under the session that started them across projects and
providers.

- POST /api/agent accepts parentSessionId (app or provider id). It is
  stored on a new session; an unknown id is a 400. On continuation it may
  be omitted, but a different parent (or the session itself) is a 400:
  the parent is fixed at creation.
- GET /api/agent/capabilities reports childSessions: true.
- Project session pages leave out children attached to an active parent
  and list them in the parent's childSessions (recursive, with their own
  provider, title, activity and project); projects report
  childSessionCount. session_upserted, pinned and archived lists carry
  parentSessionId. A fork of a child inherits its parent.
- Synchronizer upserts never write parent_session_id.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
